他八成也会买一台这种货色。
Well, I'm expecting him
to have got one of those,
to be honest.

244
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:14,960
克拉克森：
事实上，这位“大老爷”的野心
可要大得多。
CLARKSON:
In fact, His Nibs had been
rather more ambitious.

245
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,280
哈蒙德：我的天……
[大笑]
他居然搞了台928！
HAMMOND: Oh, my...
[LAUGHING]
He's got a 928!

246
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:20,680
克拉克森：那当然，货真价实的928。
CLARKSON: Absolutely, a 928.

247
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,720
我可不买那种平民保时捷。
No everyman Porsche for me.

248
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:26,400
这台车搭载的
可是4.7升V8发动机。
This one
has a 4.7-litre V8.

249
00:15:26,440 --> 00:15:27,680
梅：我还以为顶多也就是台944。
MAY: I thought a 944 at most.

250
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:31,360
先生们，隆重向你们展示
永恒的传世经典。
Gentlemen, I give you
a timeless classic.

251
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,600
一台真正的保时捷。
A proper Porsche.

252
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:37,040
杰里米，用我们那点预算
你居然能买到928？
Jeremy, you got
a 928 on our budget?

253
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:41,600
在这副褪色剥落、
残破不堪的躯壳之下，
Beneath this rather faded,
ruined exterior

254
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:43,840
跳动着一颗
纯正的关节炎心脏。
beats a heart
of pure arthritis.

255
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:46,200
- 哈蒙德：哈！那根本不可能……
- 过来瞧瞧这个。
-HAMMOND: Ha! That cannot...
-Come and have a look at this.

256
00:15:46,240 --> 00:15:47,800
快过来瞧瞧这个。
Come and have a look at this.

257
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,720
哈蒙德：
里面居然塞满了破烂！
HAMMOND:
It's even full of junk!

258
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:53,040
不不不，这些是水瓶，
算是有那么一点必不可少……
No, no, these are
the water bottles, which are
a little bit necessary...

259
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,480
哈！抓现行了吧！
Ah! Got ya!

260
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:56,480
……为了能让这玩意儿，
勉强开得动。
...in order to make it,
kind of, move.

261
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:58,920
你难道不觉得
自己有点打肿脸充胖子了吗？
Do you not think
you may have
overreached yourself a bit?

262
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:01,640
我见过挂着“拆车件”卖的
标价都比这高。
Well, I've seen one
for more than this
advertised as "Spares".

263
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:03,600
克拉克森：
行吧，我很想见识见识你们买了啥。
CLARKSON:
Well, I'd love to have a look
at what you've got.

264
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:06,040
- 其实这台看着还挺顺眼的。
- 哈蒙德：远看而已。
-This looks
quite good actually.
-HAMMOND: From a distance.

265
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:08,920
看着……简直就像
掉进过运河里一样。
Looks, it's...
It's been in a canal
at some point.

266
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:12,600
嘿，打住！
[清嗓子]
瞻仰一下这无与伦比的英姿！
Hey, now!
[CLEARS THROAT]
Survey the magnificence.

267
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:13,960
克拉克森：这台装的就是厢型车发动机。
CLARKSON: This one
has the van engine.

268
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,640
- 哈蒙德：它装的是结构优良、简单的……
- 厢型车发动机。
-HAMMOND:
It has a good, simple...
-Van engine.

269
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:18,320
我不知道你在胡扯什么。
I don't know what that is.

270
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,360
哈蒙德：
重点是我们搞到了三台保时捷！
HAMMOND:
We got three Porsche's,
that's the thing.

271
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:20,720
我们确实搞到了三台保时捷。
We did get three Porsches.

272
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:22,440
梅：破破烂烂。
克拉克森：小货车。
MAY: Pretty ropey.
CLARKSON: Van.

273
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:25,600
那是堆废铁，
我的看着还挺像样。
That's scrap,
mine looks pretty good.

274
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:27,320
来看看挑战任务是什么吧。
Let's have a look at
what the challenge is.

275
00:16:27,360 --> 00:16:29,000
能给我们信封了吗？
非常感谢。
Can we have
an envelope, please?
Thank you very much.

276
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,800
- 克拉克森：多谢。
- 噢！
-CLARKSON: Thank you.
-Ah!

277
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:34,560
“老爷车都能从伦敦开到布莱顿，
但你们行吗？”
"Veteran cars can make it
from London to Brighton,
but can you?"

278
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,120
- 不行。
- 不行，绝对……
-No.
-No. Absolutely...

279
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,000
- [众人大笑]
- 所以这根本……
但干嘛非要这么折腾？
-[ALL LAUGHING]
-So that's out of...
But why do it?

280
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:41,600
“沿途每掀开一次引擎盖，
扣五分。”
"Five points are lost
for each time you have to
open the bonnet en route."

281
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:43,040
得，这下你好几千镑没了。
Well, that's
thousands for you.

282
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:44,440
-[大笑] 噢，惨了！
-把前机盖扔了吧。
-[LAUGHING] Oh, no!
-Throw the bonnet away.

283
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,360
“前往海滨集结，
接收你们的下一项挑战，
"Rendezvous on the seafront to
receive your next challenge,

284
00:16:47,400 --> 00:16:50,200
“前提是你能开得到……
杰里米。”
"assuming you make it...
Jeremy."

285
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:53,480
-所以基本上就是从这
开着保时捷去布莱顿。
-有多远？
-So Brighton, basically,
from here in our Porsches.
-How far is that?

286
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:55,400
-按英里算的话……
-克拉克森：大概，呃，70英里。
-In miles...
-CLARKSON: It's, uh, 70 miles.

287
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:56,920
梅：我信心十足。
MAY: I'm very confident.

288
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,640
那海边见喽，伙计们。
Well, I'll see you in
the seaside then, chaps.

289
00:16:58,680 --> 00:16:59,880
见个鬼。
行了，出发！
No, you won't.
But, all right, let's go!

290
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:03,960
我仪表盘上各种报警灯
已经亮成一片了。
I've got a wide range
of warning lights on already.

291
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,560
哈蒙德：
我们正在开往……
布莱顿的路上，
HAMMOND:
We are on the way...
to Brighton

292
00:17:08,560 --> 00:17:11,480
开着我们的保时捷。
in our Porsches.

293
00:17:11,520 --> 00:17:14,560
克拉克森：
当年这车刚上市的时候，
技术可是极其前卫的。
CLARKSON:
This was a hugely advanced car
when it first came out.

294
00:17:14,600 --> 00:17:16,680
聚氨酯保险杠。
Polyurethane bumpers.

295
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:20,240
呃……史上第一款
配备被动后轮转向的车。
Um... First car ever to have
passive, rear-wheel steering.

296
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:23,080
我一直、一直都……
I've always, always...

297
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,840
天哪！我车冒汽了。
Oh, my God! I've got steam.

298
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:27,320
杰里米这是抛锚了吗？
Is Jeremy breaking down?

299
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:30,400
克拉克森：呃，伙计们，
我前机盖里正冒出
好大一团蒸汽。
CLARKSON: Uh, guys,
I've got a lot of steam
coming out of the bonnet.

300
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:33,560
他刚才说的是
“我提了点速”
还是“我冒了点汽”？
Did he say,
"I've got some speed"
or "I've got some steam"?

301
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:38,920
克拉克森：不，绝对是冒汽，
才跑了两英里
它就直接喷发了。
CLARKSON: No, it was
definitely steam and it was
erupting after just two miles.

302
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:39,960
修理厂！
Garage!

303
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:43,040
噢，老天开眼。
Oh, there is a God.

304
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:47,800
-听着，用不着加这么多。
-不用，不用，行。
-Look, it won't need all this.
-No, no. Right.

305
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,840
真全从底下漏出来了？
Is it really coming
out the bottom?

306
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:52,400
是啊，漏得比你倒进去的还快。
Yeah, it's coming out faster
than you're putting it in.

307
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:53,720
还得再来点。
Needs a bit more.

308
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,760
-杰里米？
-干嘛？
-Jeremy?
-What?

309
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:57,360
现在漏得越来越快了。
It's leaking faster
and faster now.

310
00:17:57,400 --> 00:18:00,280
克拉克森：全英格兰
有这么多水够它漏吗？
CLARKSON: Is there
this much water in England?

311
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:02,400
梅：还在往里灌呢。
MAY: And still it goes in.

312
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:05,640
所有液体
都在往外狂喷。
Every single fluid
is gushing out of it.

313
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:08,200
理查德，你能去看看
他们店里有没有鸡蛋吗？
Can you go and see if
they've got any eggs, Richard?

314
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:11,000
杰里米和理查德
进店里去买鸡蛋了，
Jeremy and Richard have
gone off inside to buy an egg,

315
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:14,280
希望能用上那个老偏方，
把蛋清混进
in the hope that we can
use that old trick
of mixing the egg white

316
00:18:14,320 --> 00:18:17,920
冷却系统里，
蛋清就会找到漏点
并堵上……
into the cooling system,
and that will find
and block...

317
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:20,640
这个。这就是哈蒙德的“杰出贡献”。
This. This is Hammond's
contribution.

318
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:22,520
他给自己买了个巧克力蛋。
He's bought himself
a chocolate egg.

319
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:23,920
-反正是蛋就管用，我只找着这个。
-塞进去。
-Well, eggs work, this
is the only one I could find.
-Put it in.

320
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:25,480
塞进去，
反正情况也不会更糟了。
Put it in,
it can't do any harm.

321
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,800
十五升，加满了。
Fifteen litres and it's full.

322
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:31,280
-你瞧见这个了吗？
-卧槽【哔——】！
-Have you seen this?
-Holy [BLEEP]!

323
00:18:31,320 --> 00:18:32,680
[两人大笑]
[BOTH LAUGHING]

324
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:34,920
又漏了一滩！
There's another puddle!

325
00:18:34,960 --> 00:18:38,440
没事，
就漏了一点点……
看，就是渗了几滴。
It's fine,
it's just a little...
Look, it's a dribble.

326
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:41,560
在把整个泰晤士河谷的水
都灌进我的冷却系统，
With all the water
from the Thames Valley
in my cooling system,

327
00:18:41,600 --> 00:18:44,800
外加一颗巧克力蛋之后，
我们终于重新上路了。
and a chocolate egg,
we were back on the road.

328
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:48,040
出发。
We're off.

329
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:51,360
得，刚才那纯粹
就是一出闹剧。
Well, that was
a complete farce.

330
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:54,040
这破车到底是在哪儿
通过车检的？
Where did this car
pass its MOT?

331
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:57,520
难道是在伊朗？
Iran, perhaps?

332
00:18:57,560 --> 00:19:00,720
我们进展还挺顺利的，
唔，大概也就开了
区区两英里吧，
Our progress was good,
for, ooh, it must have been
another two miles

333
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:06,120
接着就轮到詹姆斯爆胎，
让整个车队
被迫停下了脚步。
and then it was James's turn
to grind the convoy to a halt,
with a puncture.

334
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:09,880
伙计们，到底是谁觉得
这是个靠谱的主意？
Guys, who thought of this
was a sensible idea?

335
00:19:09,920 --> 00:19:12,800
买三辆二手保时捷，
到现在才开了四英里。
To buy three Porsches,
we've done four miles.

336
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,680
梅：不不不，开什么车都可能会爆胎的好吧。
MAY: No, no, you could have
had a puncture in any car.

337
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:17,440
-但爆胎的偏偏是你！
-[全场大笑]
-But you didn't!
-[ALL LAUGH]

338
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:20,640
后备箱根本打不开，
因为那个……
You can't open the boot,
'cause that...

339
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:22,920
[克拉克森嘟囔不清]
[CLARKSON SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY]

340
00:19:22,960 --> 00:19:26,320
克拉克森：幸好，我们给遥控后备箱开关的
残骸搭了个线。
CLARKSON: Luckily, we were
able to hot-wire the remains
of the remote boot release.

341
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:27,560
梅：有动静吗？
MAY: Anything?

342
00:19:27,960 --> 00:19:29,280
开了！
Yes!

343
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:30,720
搞定了，詹姆斯。
There you go, James.

344
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:33,360
不幸的是，备胎不仅没气，
胎纹还磨得精光。
Unfortunately, the spare
was flat and bald.

345
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:38,200
所以我们只好把原本被扎破的轮胎
带到前头的修理店去补。
So we had to take the original
punctured tyre up the road
to get it fixed.

346
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:40,240
-我的车现在运转完美。
-梅：拉倒吧，才没有。
-Mine's working perfectly now.
-MAY: No, it's not.

347
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,280
明明就很完美。
It is.

348
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:44,520
-咱俩飙车去布莱顿。
-来啊。
-I'll race you to Brighton.
-All right.

349
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:51,520
这要被扣多少分啊？
还有，我的闪电泡芙呢？
How many points off is this?
And where's my eclair?

350
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,240
他就只给了我两个。
He only gave me two.

351
00:19:53,280 --> 00:19:56,560
不幸的是，就在我胡吃海塞
巧克力泡芙的时候，
Unfortunately, while I was
gorging myself on chocolate,

352
00:19:56,600 --> 00:20:01,320
在路那头，
我的车又在排空
它身上的各种体液。
down the road,
my car was emptying itself
of yet more fluids.

353
00:20:01,360 --> 00:20:02,480
噢，我的天哪！
Ooh, my God!

354
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:03,960
-那是汽油吗？
-对啊。
-Is that petrol?
-Yeah.

355
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,280
所以，它屁股后面在漏汽油……
So, it's leaking petrol
out of the back...

356
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:08,040
-咱们是不是该站远点？
-而且，呃……
-Should we stand some
distance from it?
-And, uh...

357
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:10,520
车头还在直冒蒸汽。
There's steam coming out
of the front.

358
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:12,480
还在漏呢。
It's still leaking.

359
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:15,080
克拉克森：这或许能解释
为什么昨晚我开车来伦敦时，
CLARKSON: That might explain
the rather poor fuel
consumption I got

360
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:16,480
油耗会那么惨烈。
coming to London last night.

361
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:18,520
还有一路追着你屁股烧的那道火线。
And the trail of fire
following you.

362
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:21,600
克拉克森：谢天谢地，
布里克斯顿的热心纯爷们儿
帮我们给修好了。
CLARKSON: Happily,
the brave men of Brixton
helped us fix it.

363
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:22,880
你真是个大救星。
You're a superstar.

364
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:25,920
于是，我们再次启程。
And once again,
we were under way.

365
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:28,000
虽说进度稍微
落后了一点点。
Although, a little
behind schedule.

366
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:30,840
事实上，我们六个小时前
就出发了。
In fact, we had set off
six hours earlier.

367
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:33,400
结果现在居然还在
南伦敦晃悠，
And we were still
in South London

368
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:36,520
而且毛病还在
接二连三地出。
and things were still
going wrong.

369
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:37,920
[笑声]
这掉下来的又是啥？
[LAUGHING]
What's this?

370
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:44,760
然而正当我嘲笑詹姆斯时，
我的车又犯病了。
While I was laughing at James
though, my car went wrong
again.

371
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,800
哦，说出来你都敢信。
Oh, you're not gonna
believe it.

372
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:48,480
我的冷却液报警灯亮了。
My coolant warning light
has come on.

373
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:51,160
这破车要报废了。
It's going to break.

374
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:53,480
克拉克森：今天一早
我们向自己抛出的那个问题：
CLARKSON: The question
we'd asked ourselves
this morning

375
00:20:53,520 --> 00:20:57,160
花不到1500英镑，
到底能不能买到一辆像样的保时捷？
was whether you could
buy a decent Porsche
for less than £1,500.

376
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:59,960
答案已经
不言而喻了。
The answer was
becoming obvious.

377
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,520
[克拉克森与哈蒙德大笑]
